\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Tokenizer and detokenizer}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{language-model}
\tag{tokenization}

\p{Let #{\mathcal U} be a chosen set of texts. A \newvocab{tokenizer} is a
map
##{
\operatorname{Tok}:\mathcal U\longrightarrow\mathcal V^*.
}
A \newvocab{detokenizer} is a map
#{\operatorname{Dec}:\mathcal V^*\to\mathcal U}. We call the pair lossless on
#{\mathcal U_0\subseteq\mathcal U} when
##{
\operatorname{Dec}(\operatorname{Tok}(x))=x
\qquad(x\in\mathcal U_0).
}}

\p{SentencePiece makes lossless tokenization and a self-contained tokenizer
model explicit in \citet{secs. 3.1 and 3.5}{kudo2018sentencepiece}. Byte-pair
subword construction is described in
\citet{sec. 3.2}{sennrich2016neural}. FTIP treats the tokenizer files and their
normalization rules as part of the model interface. Different tokenizers can
represent the same text by strings of different lengths.}
